.. _getting-started-five-minutes:

Getting started in 5 minutes
============================

This walkthrough takes you from a fresh install to a three-line SCPI script.
Each step links to the full chapter if you need more detail.

1. Installation
---------------

Install PyCharm 2025.1 or newer, a Python interpreter, optionally
`RsInstrument <https://rsinstrument.readthedocs.io/en/latest/StepByStepGuide.html#installation>`_
and `R&S VISA <https://www.rohde-schwarz.com/applications/r-s-visa-application-note_56280-148812.html>`_.

Install the plugin from the Marketplace (*File → Settings → Plugins*), search ``rohde``, then restart the IDE.

.. image:: images/RsIc-menu_install_from_marketplace.drawio.png

Or use the Marketplace button:

.. raw:: html

    <p align="center"><iframe width="245px" height="48px" frameBorder="0" src="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/embeddable/install/19828"></iframe></p>

Full requirements: :doc:`Chapter_02_Installation`.

2. Add an instrument
--------------------

Open the tool window **Rohde & Schwarz Instruments** (gutter, or *View → Tool Windows*).
Click **+ Add new Instrument**, choose HiSLIP (or USB-TMC / VXI-11), enter the IP or hostname, and **Test**.

.. image:: images/RsIc-add_new_instrument_success.drawio.png

Keep the **Alias** (for example ``smw``). You will use it in scripts.

Details: :ref:`adding-your-first-instrument`.

3. Send a query
---------------

Open the Instrument Tool Window from the instrument panel (or right-click → **Open in Extra Window**).
Connect, type ``*IDN?`` in the SCPI command field, and send.

.. image:: images/RsIcITW-comm_panel.drawio.png

The identification string appears in the response field.

Details: :doc:`Chapter_06_InstrumentsToolWindow`.

4. Read the SCPI Tree
---------------------

Stay connected. Open the **SCPI Tree** tab and **Read Tree from Instrument**.
Do this once per firmware; the tree is then cached and drives auto-completion and search.

.. image:: images/FunctionPanel_ScpiTree-read_scpi_tree.drawio.png

Details: :doc:`Chapter_07_FunctionPanel_ScpiTree`.

5. A short script in the multi-line SCPI editor
-----------------------------------------------

On the communicator, open the **Multi-line SCPI Editor**. Enter:

.. code-block:: console

    *RST
    *OPC?
    *IDN?

Press **F5** (execute all). Responses show as inlays. **F4** runs the current line.

.. image:: images/RsIcScpiScripts-ml_run_whole_script_result.drawio.png

The bound editor is stored with the instrument (command banks). For a project ``.scpi`` file, use *New → SCPI File*.

Details: :doc:`Chapter_13_PlainScpiScripts`.
